{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Business Diagram Stages "}, {"type": "position", "content": 8}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "A1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about business process diagram."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Gives information about instruments for data collection. Apply methods for data collection, designing the necessary instruments for information processing, according to the situation set by the company."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level.  Recognizes basic ideas on IT concepts, systems theory, and diagrams of processes."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Verb Can for Permission"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use the modal verb <span class=\"strong\">can</span> to ask for <span class=\"strong\">permission</span>. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you want to ask for <span class=\"strong\">permission</span> to do something, you usually use <span class=\"strong\">can</span>. Remember that can is a modal verb, therefore, you do not need to conjugate this verb depending on the subject. <br/><br/>  In order to create sentences to ask for <span class=\"strong\">permission</span>, you can follow the next structure:<br/><br/>  <div class=\"center_text\"><span class=\"strong\">Can</span> + subject + verb + complement + ?</div><br/><br/>   Examples:<br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Can</span> I create an initial diagram?<br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Can</span> she gather the additional requirements?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Really? Can I help?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Can we go over those stages in detail before we start?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Can I obtain information from different areas of the company?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "How to Diagram a Business Process"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "A business process diagram is a graphic representation of a series of steps that seek to achieve a company's goal. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are three stages to diagram a business process:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "1. Generate a simple diagram based on the initial talks and meetings."}, {"type": "text", "content": "2. Bring together the additional requirements."}, {"type": "text", "content": "3. Include the requirements in the diagram."}, {"type": "text", "content": "It is advisable to repeat steps number one and two until everybody agrees on the diagram and what it shows."}, {"type": "example", "content": "There are three stages to diagram the business process."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Get the additional requirements!"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "preliminary "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "previous; something that introduces a procedure "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: First, create a preliminary diagram that contains a general overview of the process."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob08aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "overview "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "summary or general outline of something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: First, create a preliminary diagram of a general overview of the process."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob08aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "upfront "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in advance or in front of a situation "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That's what we call the upfront discovery."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob08aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "stage "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a step in a process"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: At this stage, stop and ask yourself important questions."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob08aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hesitate "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to doubt or give second thoughts"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Make sure to use the proper terminology and don't hesitate to make changes if you need."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob08aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about business diagrams on internet."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Describe the stages people follow to make a business diagram."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Compare the stages with the ones you learned in this learning material."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share it with a partner."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I look for specific information on the internet."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I describe the stages I found on the internet."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I compare between the stages I found on the internet and the stages I learned in this learning material."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "id": 0, "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome", "template_override": 1}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n1le02ob08re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe8n1le02ob08re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Jefferson</span>: Hello, Andrea. What are you doing? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Andrea</span>: Hi! I have to draw a business process diagram. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Jefferson</span>:  Really? Can I help? I want to learn how to create those types of diagrams. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Andrea</span>:  Sure! As you know, we use these diagrams to describe a roadmap for the implementation of a set of activities. These activities help the company achieve a specific goal.  In order to draw it, we need to follow three stages.<br/>"}, {"time": "25500", "image": "enpe8n1le02ob08re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Jefferson</span>: Can we go over those stages in detail before we start? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Andrea</span>: No problem. First, create a preliminary diagram that contains a general overview of the process. To do that, use information from previous meetings, managers, and stakeholders. That's what we call the upfront discovery. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Jefferson</span>:  Can I obtain information from different areas of the company? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Andrea</span>: That's the second stage. You need to gather additional requirements. To do so, speak with every person involved in each phase of the process. In this stage, you may find that some employees don't follow established procedures.  <br/>"}, {"time": "62500", "image": "enpe8n1le02ob08re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Jefferson</span>: And, Can I include all that information on the diagram? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Andrea</span>:  At this stage, stop and ask yourself important questions such as:  what's the overall goal of the business process? When does the process start? When does it finish? Make sure to use the proper terminology and don't hesitate to make changes if you need.  <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Jefferson</span>:  What's the third stage? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Andrea</span>: When you get to the third stage, include all the requirements on the diagram. Make sure the information is very detailed and easy to read. After that, show your diagram to other people and repeat stages two and three until everyone is happy with the results.  <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Jefferson</span>:  Thanks a lot, Andrea."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n1le02ob08re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can describe how to draw a business process diagram."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about the three stages to consider to diagram the business process."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can give advice about how to develop each stage."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How do you usually create a plan to achieve something?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Why is it important for companies to achieve their goals?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Taking into Account All Types of Potential Scenarios"}], "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "img_path": ""}, {"stimuli_ids": [1], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "type": "question"}], "responses": [{"_d